    "title": "Firefighter hospitalized, residents displaced after Hartford apartment fire - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By William Gonzalez ,\n1 hours ago HARTFORD, Conn. (WTNH) — One firefighter is in the hospital and multiple people are displaced after an apartment building fire in Hartford.\nAccording to the Hartford Police Department, crews responded to an apartment building at the intersection of Hudson Street and Park Street in the city’s South Green neighborhood at around 9:34 p.m. on Wednesday for a report of a three-alarm fire.\nPhoto: WTNH Photo: WTNH Pedestrian killed in crash in New Haven When the crews arrived, they saw that the building’s second and third floors were fully engulfed in flames. Two firefighters fell through the floor on the third floor of the building, one was taken to the hospital and neither are seriously injured.\nThere were no injuries to any civilians, but multiple people will be displaced by the fire. The department said that the Special Services Unit will help with relocation.\nThis is a developing story, stay with News 8 for updates.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WTNH.com.\n3",
